from crashing a political conference to  kidnapping a TV star there's nothing  that's off limits for Sasha Baron Cohen  and  all right  one of the most iconic moments in the  first Borat movie is probably already  burned into your mind for how perfectly  it captured American culture in the mid  odds in this scene Borat somehow manages  to get a real Rodeo to agree to him  singing the National Anthem before a  show this was during a difficult time in  American history the war in Iraq was at  its peak and then President George W  Bush was a very controversial figure in  political discourse since this scene  took place at a rodeo in Virginia it  should come as no surprise that borat's  audience was definitely leaning  conservative this moment is incredible  for a number of reasons dressed in an  over-the-top patriotic Ensemble Borat  gets the audience wild up by declaring  his enthusiastic support for what he  calls the United States war of Terror  you should drink the blood of every  single man woman and child of Iraq  of course things go truly off the rails  when Borat decides to change the words  to The Star-Spangled Banner to say that  every country that isn't Kazakhstan is  run by little girls the crowd was so  enraged that Sasha Baron Cohen had to be  escorted out of the venue for his own  safety a scene that didn't end up  included in the final film borat's Rodeo  stunt is a perfect example of how Baron  Cohen is willing to put himself in real  danger just to get a reaction  in the sequel to Borat called Borat  subsequent movie film Sasha Baron Cohen  makes an effort to comment directly on  contemporary social and political issues  following the 2016 election Borat ends  up in a number of situations that  reflect on the rise in discrimination  and racism in American culture one  interaction that stands out in the  sequel is when Borat and his daughter  tutar played by Maria bakalova go  shopping for a cage that she must live  in Baron Cohen's intention for the scene  was likely to comment on the ongoing  discrimination against immigrants as the  United States government was keeping  undocumented immigrants in cages despite  the bizarre scenario the store owner  doesn't seem to mind that Borat is  intending to keep his daughter in a cage  instead going along with the whole  ordeal at one point in the sales process  Borat even brings up Donald Trump's  immigration policy which seems to get a  positive reaction but I hear McDonald  Trump yes  it's a perfect example of Baron Cohen's  method of getting people to say exactly  what they're thinking  yet another hilarious scene in the  original Borat comes when Borat learns  how to drive learning to drive is an  essential rite of passage for many  American youths which is why it was a  perfect choice by Sasha Baron Cohen to  put Borat in such a situation paired up  with instructor Michael snitzka Borat  completely fails to comprehend the  nuances of driving while pushing his  teacher's buttons in the process  starting out with an awkward kiss on the  cheek borat's time in the driver's seat  makes for an unforgettably  cringe-inducing sequence once their  conversation devolves into a discussion  about consent and women's rights things  get wild in true Borat fashion the woman  has a right to choose who she has sex  with what how about that there must be  consent  unlike many of the strangers Borat meets  who aren't afraid to express offensive  beliefs his driving instructor tries to  guide him towards doing the right thing  I like you do you like me I do like you  you are my friend you're a nice young  man and I am your friend  as far as men on the street comedy goes  it's hard to beat the subway sequence  near the beginning of the first Borat  film borat's encounters with the  denizens of New York City are simply  hilarious regardless of the context of  who Borat is or where he is from Sasha  Baron Cohen seems to enjoy putting  himself in cringe-worthy situations so  his actions on the subway in this scene  make for an excellent introduction to  borat's time in America First Borat  attempts to kiss several innocent  bystanders taking public transit as a  way of introducing himself this goes  rather poorly of course if that wasn't  enough Borat accidentally lets loose a  live chicken within the crowded subway  car to cause the maximum amount of chaos  only in New York  one highlight of Borat subsequent movie  film is without a doubt the risky prank  pulled during former vice president Mike  Pence's speech at the conservative  political action conference the  conference also known as CPAC has become  an essential yearly event for the  Republican Party Sasha Baron Cohen has  never hidden his left-wing sensibilities  so his desire to cause chaos at CPAC  shouldn't come as a surprise to fans in  the context of the movie Borat  desperately wants to give away his  daughter as a gift to president Donald  Trump at the behest of the president of  Kazakhstan who respects Trump's approach  to governance and wants to be a part of  the club since Borat cannot approach the  sitting U.S president he settles for  giving away his daughter to Pence  instead during his CPAC speech Borat  dresses up as Donald Trump and  infiltrates the event but he causes a  ridiculous Ruckus when he starts yelling  at Pence on stage  I brought the girl for you  Baron Cohen is openly not a fan of trump  as he has expressed on Twitter so  dressing up as him through his Borat  character uses several layers of irony  to criticize the Republican Party  Sasha Baron Cohen doesn't need to rely  on raunchy or political humor to get a  laugh in the original 2006 Borat one of  the funniest moments is a G-rated gag  that anyone who's read Dr Seuss can  appreciate in one very brief scene Borat  visits the Exotic Wildlife dealers at  Munch ranch when presented with a  certain slow-moving reptile the  journalist doesn't seem to recognize the  creature what type of dog is this this  is a tortoise the patience of the two  employees featured in this scene is  truly quite admirable is this a cat in a  hat no it's a tortoise and a shell yes  this scene has become a favorite among  Borat fans for its simple premise and  hysterical delivery  borat's relationship with his daughter  tutar is the heart and soul of borat's  subsequent movie film with a surprising  amount of character growth for the  titular reporter while he is constantly  putting his loving daughter into  troubling situations Borat and tutar  grow closer and closer with each absurd  encounter when Borat brings tutar to a  southern debutant ball in Disguise he  goes in with the intention of presenting  her as a proper young lady as you can  imagine this doesn't sit well with the  other guests what unfolds is a standout  moment in the film in which Borat and  tutar under the fake names Sandra  Jessica Parker Drummond and Professor  Philip drumon III do what they claim is  a traditional Kazakh fertility dance the  dance involves showing a room full of  Stuffy Southern Aristocrats tutar's  blood-stained underwear which they  respond to by awkwardly clapping this  mockery of high society in the south is  genuinely hilarious and the dance itself  is surprisingly well choreographed and  executed by the two stars the running  joke at the heart of Borat is the  journalist's obsession with Baywatch  actress Pamela Anderson after seeing her  on television Borat falls deeply in love  with her and throughout his hijinks he  continues to bring up his desire to find  her and make her his wife  Having learned the many lessons from us  and day  I will now teach America how to have a  wedding kazaki style  this plot line finally ends with the  failed kidnapping attempt by Borat who  tries to put a traditional marriage sack  over Anderson's head while this may  sound horrifying it turns out that  Pamela Anderson was in on the joke all  along according to the Daily Beast Sasha  Baron Cohen made sure to get Anderson's  approval ahead of time the comedian told  the outlet the first time we did it at a  book signing and I grabbed her over my  shoulder and ran out with her and no one  did anything I was like what kind of  fans are these so we did it again and  they started running after me however  there were definitely some unintended  consequences to Anderson's role in Borat  Baron Cohen explained that Anderson's  then husband Kid Rock ended up divorcing  her over the entire thing he elaborated  I thought it was a joke but then a few  weeks later they got divorced and they  put as a reason for divorce Borat  the Borat subsequent movie film scene  that got the most press attention after  release was centered around former New  York city mayor Rudy Giuliani in keeping  with Sasha Baron Cohen's desire to mess  with Republican political figures he and  his team came up with the idea to  disguise Maria bakalova as a  conservative journalist who attempts to  seduce Giuliani on camera in the context  of the story this is actually a low  point for Borat and tutar Borat has had  a change of heart about his daughter  after realizing how much he actually  loves her meanwhile tutar has decided to  proceed with the seduction plan in order  to win his approval what unfolds is a  shockingly disturbing scene in which  Giuliani seems to accept the seduction  attempt despite the fact that he was  under the impression that tutar is  underage this was a seemingly genuine  act on giuliani's part as he had no idea  he was in a Borat film until it was too  late his unacceptable Behavior became  the center of the political news cycle  for some time  [Music]
 

